title: Creation of the Cheka
new-page: true
view-if: coalition_government = 1 and cheka_founded = 0
max-visits: 1
tags: event

= Constituent Assembly Protests

With the advent of a coalition government, there are some within the Bolshevik leadership who fear the non-Bolshevik commissars will now impede our anti-counterrevolutionary efforts, through legal and governmental meddling. In particular, hardline Bolsheviks within the Military Revolutionary Committee have petitioned for some kind of special commission, to take up their work free from outside interference. 

It has been proposed that we create an "Extraordinary Commission for Combating Counter-Revolution and Sabotage" (Cheka), which will inherit the functions of the Military Revolutionary Committee. 

  
- @create
- @reject


  @create
  title: Create the Extraordinary Commission. 
  on-arrival: {!
    Q.cheka_founded = 1; instability += 1; 
    Q.cheka = 5; Q.cheka_strength = 5; Q.cheka_militancy = 0.2; 
    Q.internal_expend += 0.25; cheka_strength = 5; 
    Q.city_militia_strength -= 5; Q.crime -= 5; 
    Q.moderate_dissent += 5; Q.leftcom_dissent -= 10; Q.leninist_dissent -= 5;
    Q.leftcom_strength += 5; Q.leninist_strength += 2;
    Q.intelligentsia_unrest += 5; Q.elite_unrest += 5;
!}

We have created the Extraordinary Commission. It gets to work monitoring known enemies of the Revolution. 


@reject
title: We have no need for such a thing. 
on-arrival: {!
    Q.moderate_dissent -= 2; Q.leftcom_dissent += 10; Q.leninist_dissent += 5;
    Q.leftcom_strength -= 2; 
!}

The proposal is rejected. The more militant Bolsheviks are extremely displeased.
